Chapter 10: "The Kingdom of the Lion King"
Chapter 10-22: "Preparatory Moves and Refusal"

---

—This occurred at the same time Natsuki Subaru, in the "Six Tongues" hideout, was told about the dreadnought-class calamity afflicting the Kingdom of Lugunica; a scene in the commercial district of the Royal Capital of Lugunica.

---

"—By some means or another, the enemy has already seized the Dragon History Stone and taken complete control. That is the situation the Royal Castle finds itself in now. I've filled in the gaps in the information with my own speculation, but I doubt I'm far off the mark."

"...Indeed. It would also explain why we're being hounded right now. At the very least, we should consider the chain of command at the Royal Castle to be under their control."

"— —"

"Garfiel, are you alright?"

"Eh? O-Oh, I'm fine... Nah, honestly, talk's on a scale I never even thought about, so... I just dunno what to say."

Shaking his head, Garfiel revealed his all-too-honest feelings. But Otto empathized with his younger brother-in-arms, knowing it couldn't be helped.

"...Given the situation, after all."

To be frank, Otto himself was equally plagued by confusion and bewilderment. The only difference was their roles within the camp; Otto was simply not allowed to stop thinking.

In this dire situation, Garfiel had done his duty well. —No, it wasn't just Garfiel. It was the result of everyone working together as one, giving it their all.
The only one who failed was himself, who had his weapon taken away so pathetically.

"—Tch."

Leaning against the wall, sitting with one knee drawn up, Garfiel groaned in pain from his throat.
The deep exhaustion and pain that wouldn't fade from his face was unthinkable for Garfiel, who possessed extraordinary toughness and recovery power. It spoke to just how extraordinary and absurd the power of the one who landed that blow on him—Reinhard—truly was.

—It had been some time since Reinhard had stood in Otto's way, and they had barely managed to break through using every card they had.

The battle had lasted less than a minute, but by the end, everyone was battered and bruised. Garfiel, who had engaged Reinhard in a direct confrontation, was in a particularly terrible state. Otto felt pathetic; even after deliberately luring the enemy into carelessness, he was incapacitated just from a blow grazing his chin.

The victory they had somehow scraped together—and it was only thanks to unexpected reinforcements—and the fact that they were even brought to that situation in the first place, left Otto with far too much to reflect on.
The only reason they could even have something resembling a debriefing was because the reinforcements who met up with them had led them here, securing them a momentary safe haven.

"—Just managing to shake that one off is a feat in itself. Even if it was a role forced upon him, a hundred ordinary soldiers wouldn't be able to lay a finger on him."

"But, for that, we had to make her play a card she shouldn't have had to play. What she was forced to let go from her life is significant. I cannot forgive that person."

"...Your indignation is likely justified. I'm sure he's prepared to be resented. That is what it means to be the 'Sword Saint'. I myself have never lost my anger towards the 'Sword Saint'."

"That is..."

Otto narrowed his eyes quietly at the man who placed a large hand on his own bald head.
What he was about to say—whether a question or speculation—he bit his tongue, aware that he had already let slip something he shouldn't have.

However—

"—You are speaking of anger towards my wife, not Reinhard, aren't you."

Instead of Otto, who had fallen silent, the old swordsman—Wilhelm—entered through the door and took those words with a tone of certainty.

Wilhelm came into the room, bringing Rem and an elderly man with short hair with him. He first let Rem inside, then turned to the man,

"Conwood, I'm sorry for the trouble. I'm in your debt for hiding us."

"Hah, to have Wilhelm Trias—the man who was the very embodiment of arrogance and selfishness—thank me so admirably... It might just rain tomorrow."

"You..."

"It's a joke. —And besides, it's only natural. It's the natural thing to do, Wilhelm. Me lending you my strength... that's a given, no need for thanks."

"— —"

After the familiar tone, the man’s voice trembled, and Wilhelm's cheeks stiffened.
The man relaxed his cheeks, seeming to find his old friend's reaction amusing, then looked at Otto and Garfiel inside the room.

"I owe a debt to your comrade, Natsuki Subaru-dono, from the White Whale hunt. A debt so huge it'd take a lifetime to repay. I won't let anyone through here, so rest easy."

"...Shopkeeper, you have my gratitude."

"I told you. My gratitude is far greater. ...No one believes Natsuki Subaru-dono is part of the Witch's Cult. It's the same with Crusch-sama."

Saying that, the man clapped Wilhelm on the shoulder and left the room, closing the door. Watching his back disappear behind the door, Otto called out, "Rem-san."

The place they had reached, guided by Wilhelm, was a private room in a tavern offered as a shelter. While Otto and the others explained the situation in this room, Rem had been in a separate room.
The reason was—

"Are Petra-chan and the others alright?"

"...For now, they're resting. Petra-chan was quite distraught, and Meili-chan ended up being the one to soothe her... but they've both fallen asleep."

"I see... Understood. Thank you."

"No, I didn't do anything. More importantly, what about the discussion?"

"—We've just finished confirming the current situation, I suppose."

Otto directed his pale blue eyes to the back of the room and answered a tense-looking Rem.
Following her gaze, there stood a large figure, seated in a private room chair yet still with his head higher than Otto or Wilhelm.

A giant of advanced age with a bald head and sun-darkened skin, his name was—

"—Barga Cromwell. Formerly one of the primary figures who escalated the kingdom's civil war."

"...Unfortunately, I have no idea who you're talking about. I'm just Old Man Rom, an oversized geezer living in the slums, nothing more."

"How brazen. What about the scar on my chest that I gouged out? Are you hiding it under that great bushy white chest hair of yours?"

"I have even less idea what you mean. Not that it concerns me, but I'd rather not get old. To think even the renowned 'Sword Demon' can't match the passage of years with his wits."

"You bastard—"

"...Both of you, please stop fighting. Petra-chan and the others are resting upstairs. Don't we have no time for infighting?"

Rem stepped forward, as if cutting between the two at odds, and glared at them alternately. Faced with her stern gaze, Wilhelm bowed his head, and the giant figure—the old giant who called himself Old Man Rom—also cleared his throat and showed an attitude of compliance towards Rem.

While grateful for Rem's intervention and judgment, Otto couldn't help but feel a certain sense of understanding regarding the hostile exchange between those two.

—Otto was also a citizen of this Dragonfriend Kingdom of Lugunica.
He knew the facts: 'Sword Demon' Wilhelm van Astrea was a hero of the 'Demi-Human War', and Barga Cromwell was one of those who commanded the Demi-Human Alliance during that civil war.

He never imagined that Barga Cromwell was still alive.
Of course, the man himself—Old Man Rom—denied any connection to Barga, and would likely never admit it.

At any rate—

"I'll call you Rom-san... Thank you for sending Wilhelm-san as reinforcements. Without that, we would have been annihilated by now."

"I doubt you could call that an exaggeration. In your current state, if you were captured by the castle—not being a royal selection candidate or a knight—they could make you disappear however they like and cover it up."

"Make us disappear, how could they..."

"We must consider the worst possibilities. Even if we dislike it and flee to optimism, there's no reason the enemy would go easy on us. ...Especially now that Miklotov is dead."

Rem was at a loss for words at Old Man Rom's grave assessment, but Otto agreed.
Always assume the worst. Ultimately, that's what leads to finding a way out of a desperate situation. Even he himself thinks it’s pessimism.

"Yo, Wilhelm-san, you saved my ass earlier."

At that moment, Garfiel, sitting against the wall, raised a hand lightly towards Wilhelm. At his call, Wilhelm turned, "Garfiel-dono,"

"In that situation, my skill was insufficient; my apologies. I had to surprise him by aiming to cut you as well, otherwise I could not have reached Reinhard with my sword."

"That was somethin' I was ready for when I took it on, so no worries. That wound's already mostly closed up. ...The 'Sword Saint's' hand strike, though... still nowhere near healed."

"— —"

"More 'mportantly, what were ya doin', Wilhelm-san? I hear our boss 'n that Duchess were escapin' together..."

"Indeed. Let me tell you what happened on my side."

With that, Wilhelm began to calmly recount the circumstances surrounding himself and his master, Crusch.

"After Subaru-dono and Emilia-sama visited the mansion and departed, Crusch-sama, having seen them off, secluded herself in her room. Of course, none of the household, myself included, could approach her, and she was not even taking proper meals."

"That must have been... worrying."

"Indeed. Everyone knew things couldn't continue that way. So, I left the mansion to prepare for requesting assistance from Crusch-sama's father, the former Duke, Meckart Karsten-sama. However, during my absence—"

"—Crusch-sama left the mansion alone and headed for the residence of Lord Miklotov McMahon."

"That's correct. By the time word reached my ears, it was already too late."

With an expression of deep regret, Wilhelm lamented his own inadequacy.
But if Crusch had deliberately waited for Wilhelm's absence, it was only a matter of sooner or later, and there was no reason he should be blamed.
Though, given the resulting situation, the 'Sword Demon's' self-reproach was understandable.

"Naturally, it is unthinkable that Crusch-sama would commit such a reckless act. I immediately went up to the Royal Castle and appealed to an old acquaintance, Lord Bordeaux Zellgef. However, not only would he not listen, but on my way back, I ended up being pursued by soldiers. That's when—"

"—I called out to him. Frankly, it was a bitter choice for me as well."

"...It was also not my intention to cut down Kingdom soldiers by force and break through. When I saw this man in a lit place, I doubted my own eyes."

"Both of you."

The inerasable anger and old grudges inevitably laced their words with venom.
While watching the men being gently rebuked by Rem, Otto understood the circumstances of their meeting. And how Wilhelm came to join them.

"That being the case, what about you, Rom-san? It seems you were remarkably well-prepared, or rather, quick to act."

"It's natural for you to be suspicious, but I was only able to move just before things happened, much like yourselves. I only noticed because my nose is sharp... Since long ago, I've had a sense for approaching danger. It's been rusty for a while, but the recent turmoil seems to have knocked the rust off."

"I see. —Understood."

Otto didn't press further on Old Man Rom, who rolled his large shoulders and answered matter-of-factly.
Ultimately, they were only facing the same direction at this moment; their positions were fundamentally opposed. It was only natural for him to keep his cards hidden, and to blame him for it would be narrow-minded.

At the very least, Old Man Rom's actions had saved Otto and the others from a pinch. For now, appreciating that action should take precedence over doubting his true intentions.

"You're a scary young man. Your eyes aren't smiling at all."

"Sorry. Merchants are supposed to smile in public and chuckle inwardly in private, but lately, I've had trouble acting very merchant-like. Even I find it distasteful. —Though, if being a good-natured merchant means letting one's own people die, then such a person is unnecessary right now."

"— —"

"...Sorry, I spoke out of turn."

After shrugging and replying, Otto chastised himself for the unnecessary words.
Keeping it to his thoughts was one thing, but once spoken, words are as good as a weapon. If one suddenly draws a weapon while facing someone, they can't complain about being stabbed repeatedly.

As he suspected, being overcome in his 'Divine Protection of Word Soul' was affecting him more than he realized. He had always warned himself, like a curse, that entrusting his identity to his Divine Protection was dangerous, but recently he had relied on it too much. This was the price.

"—Anyway, our positions here are the same. Our masters have been unjustly defamed, and the Royal Castle tacitly approves... no, is actively leading it. The objective is to eliminate the royal selection candidates, destroy the very rules of the royal selection, and rule the kingdom."

"And for that, Emilia-san and that person are being slandered... The ones Wilhelm-san and Rom-san support are, too, is that it?"

"Emilia-sama, Felt-sama, and the Duchess... that means the only ones left are Anastasia-sama and the Church's new candidate, Feltore-sama."

"I wonder about that. If the 'Sage Council' and the participants of the half-round table are unscrupulous, there are any number of ways to defame Anastasia-sama. Since Anastasia-sama is from Kararagi, they could say she's plotting to have the city-state invade the Kingdom... Or perhaps, that she colluded with Emilia-sama in the Vollachia Empire to assassinate Priscilla-sama—"

"—Enough! Don't joke about that!"

At Otto's prediction of vicious scenarios, Rem raised her voice in anger.
Her pale blue eyes moist, breathing heavily, she clenched her fists tightly, enraged at the slanderous talk of Priscilla's death that Otto had speculated on.

"I will absolutely not allow Priscilla-san's, that person's death to be defiled and used! If they seriously say such things, I will not forgive it...! If it reaches Abel-san's ears, it will be war with Vollachia!"

"In reality, it's no laughing matter. Coldly treating Emilia-sama, who brought back results that could lead to a friendship treaty with the Empire, is tantamount to throwing mud in the face of the Empire that recognized Emilia-sama. It's a foolish reason for war, but history is full of foolish reasons for starting wars. And besides..."

"—Even if it comes to war, Reinhard is there. Controlling the Royal Castle means being able to move the 'Sword Saint'. Until now, the authority to issue orders to the 'Sword Saint' seems to have been strictly controlled to prevent that... but the enemy has gotten their hands on it."

"That can't... be..."

Though it was truly the worst possibility, Old Man Rom didn't deny Otto's thoughts, and instead paved over the nightmare by filling in the missing parts.
The horror was so great that Rem and Garfiel, who had just risked their lives to evade a single bout with Reinhard, were speechless.

Only one person—

"—So it is the 'Divine Protection of the Sword Saint' after all."

—The 'Sword Demon' muttered at a volume almost no one could hear.

"...Judging from the situation, the enemy clearly intends to attack the royal selection. That being the case, we must consider Filtore-sama, who recently appeared on the stage, and the 'Dragon Church' that supports her, to be on the enemy's side. Just to confirm, regarding the princess who disappeared fifteen years ago—"

"—Felt is Felt. There is no other answer."

Hating how the silence was stagnating the discussion, Otto tried to organize the situation and confirm facts, but Old Man Rom's words cut him off hard and clear.
As if realizing that a simple denial overlaying a question was unfriendly, Old Man Rom added, "However," to the surrounding eyes,

"The story that the 'Dragon Church' was sheltering the missing princess seems dubious at best. Even if they kept their distance from the Royal Castle, staying silent about that fact for over a year since the royal selection started... in the face of a crisis threatening the kingdom's very existence, that's unthinkable."

Balancing a firm opinion with an uncertain attitude, Old Man Rom was clearly hiding something.
Naturally, the sharpness in the 'Sword Demon's' eyes directed at the old giant intensified.

"— —"

Wilhelm, who had been the commander of the Royal Guard fifteen years ago, was also said to have been the person in charge of searching for the missing princess. His desire to know the truth about the princess suspicions cast on Felt and Filtore this time must have been stronger than anyone's.
However, the mental fortitude of the man suspected of being one of the three great heads of the Demi-Human Alliance was not so weak as to crack under the obsession dwelling in that gaze.

At any rate—

"...I understand how bad the situation is."

Exhaling a small breath, Rem straightened her back firmly, as if forcing a change of mood. She then looked around the room at the faces of Otto and the others,

"Frankly, I'm very worried about that person who isn't here, but Emilia-san and Sister in the castle are in danger, right? How on earth do we get those two... no, Felt-san as well. How do we get them out?"

"With Reinhard and the Knight Commander over there, a frontal assault's way too reckless no matter how ya look at it. It'd be like 'Gaddogi Guaddo Zeadd's Mountain Retreat'. We need a plan, Otto-nii."

Garfiel, heavily burdened from the fight with Reinhard, agreed with Rem and looked to Otto with eyes expecting a plan.
Both of them were undoubtedly worried about Emilia confined in the castle, and even more so about Ram, who accompanied her as her attendant.
It was truly heartbreaking to tell them this, but—

"—No. We will prioritize escaping from the Royal Capital. We don't have the leeway to extract Emilia-sama and Ram-san, or Felt-sama, from the Royal Castle."

"Wha—!?"

Eyes widening in shock, Garfiel and Rem raised their voices simultaneously. Garfiel put a hand on the wall and stood up, barking, "Otto-nii!"

"Escape... Ya mean we ain't goin' to help 'em?! What's that supposed to mean!"

"It means exactly what I said. Currently, we have neither the means nor the fighting strength to extract Emilia-sama and the others who are imprisoned in the castle. Any half-baked plan would be crushed by force, and we would all simply fall into enemy hands together. We cannot afford such a losing battle."

"A losing battle... But, Sister and Emilia-san are there..."

"I understand. But even if the enemy has already seized the Royal Castle, they cannot easily lay a hand on the royal selection candidates. Even Reinhard-san, who is their puppet, wouldn't be able to overlook such a move. Their freedom will be restricted, but as long as they are in the castle, there's a high possibility that Emilia-sama and the others won't be harmed. That's my assessment."

"B-But still..."

While Otto remained as calm as possible, careful not to let emotion into his voice, Garfiel and Rem, their feelings exposed, were greatly agitated. However, Old Man Rom raised a large hand and interjected into their exchange, "May I?"

"I agree with that youngster. Even if they're in the castle, I'll find a way to manage things with Felt and the others. What's scarier is giving them an excuse by our own actions. Their position has already worsened with that mabeast incident. We'd like to avoid making it worse if we can."

"Even you, Old Man Rom, agree with Otto-san? ...What about you, Wilhelm-san?"

"—I understand your feelings, Rem-dono, being worried about your master and sister. However, challenging a fully prepared opponent while resigned to disadvantage is a fool's errand... It vexes me, but Barga has a point."

At Wilhelm's answer, slowly shaking his head, Rem bit her lip.
